 critique from Ranjan et al. (2018).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_002\",\n      \"name\": \"Aza-Michael addition of ammonia to acrylonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_005\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"neutral to basic; stream/pool\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Nucleophilic attack of NH3 on the activated double bond forms \u03b2-aminopropionitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Explicit step in the cyanosulfidic photoredox sequence (Patel et al., 2015).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_003\",\n      \"name\": \"Photoreductive conversion to cyanohydrin and formation of \u03b1-hydroxythioamide\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_001\", \"mol_011\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_009\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV\", \"HS\u2212 (from NaHS)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"UV 254 nm, presence of HS\u2212\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Successive UV/HS\u2212 reductions convert nitrile to aldehyde, trap as cyanohydrin, deliver HS\u2212 for cyclization to \u03b3-butyrothiolactam.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Based on Patel et al. (2015); need for HS\u2212 and UV, environmental critique by Ranjan et al. (2018).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_004\",\n      \"name\": \"Photoredox cyclization and reduction to proline \u03b1-aminonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_009\", \"mol_001\", \"mol_011\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_008\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": [\"UV\", \"HS\u2212 (from NaHS)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"UV 254 nm, staged HS\u2212 delivery\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Further photoreduction and cyclization form pyrrolidine structure; HCN addition gives \u03b1-aminonitrile.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Final mechanistic step before hydrolysis in Patel et al. (2015); 32% yield over final two steps. Critiques as above.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_005\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrolysis of proline \u03b1-aminonitrile to proline via prolinamide\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_008\", \"mol_023\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_026\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Biochemical\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-370K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"acidic or near-neutral water\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Slow aqueous hydrolysis of \u03b1-aminonitrile via amide to proline.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Hydrolysis step not reported in Patel et al. (2015); implied in classic Strecker chemistry. (Ritson, 2021; speculative for proline yield)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrolysis of prolinamide to proline\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_026\", \"mol_023\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_027\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Biochemical\",\n      \"agents\": [null],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-370K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"ambient\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"hot spring/evaporative pond\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Aqueous hydrolysis of prolinamide to proline.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"General amide hydrolysis; classic Strecker sequence. No measured prebiotic hydrolysis yield for proline. (Patel et al., 2015; Ritson, 2021)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_007\",\n      \"name\": \"Physical phase/solution amplification