thway in Patel et al. (2015); presence of cyanamide reduces proline pathway efficiency.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pathways\": [\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyanosulfidic surface photoredox pathway to proline (Patel route)\",\n      \"description\": \"Stepwise assembly from HCN and acetylene via acrylonitrile, aza-Michael addition, successive photoreductions and cyclization to proline \u03b1-aminonitrile, then hydrolysis and phase amplification to L-proline.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_004\", \"mol_005\", \"mol_009\", \"mol_008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"name\": \"Spark discharge (Strecker) surface pathway to racemic proline\",\n      \"description\": \"Electric discharge in reducing atmosphere yields amino acids including racemic proline; chirality resolved later.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_013\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_027\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"name\": \"Extraterrestrial delivery via photoprocessed ices and meteorite/asteroid alteration\",\n      \"description\": \"Photoprocessing of ices produces organic residues hydrolyzed on parent bodies or Earth surface, yielding racemic proline; chirality resolved in amplification.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_014\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_027\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"name\": \"Parent body aqueous alteration route to proline\",\n      \"description\": \"HCN and ammonia in meteoritic parent bodies processed hydrothermally to release proline.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_015\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_027\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"name\": \"Hydrothermal protometabolic route (Glu \u2192 GSA \u2192 P5C \u2192 proline, speculative