e]\n  - rxn_012: mol_001, mol_003, mol_021 -> mol_022 (Parent-body aqueous alteration (Strecker/fischer\u2013tropsch)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_013: mol_005, mol_013 -> mol_014 (Cyanamide guanidinylation (competing arginine branch)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_014: mol_014, mol_021 -> mol_020 (Hydrolysis of arginine \u03b1-aminonitrile to arginine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_015: mol_015, mol_003 -> mol_016 (Reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate to glutamate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_016: mol_016 -> mol_017 (Reduction of glutamate to glutamate-5-semialdehyde (hypothetical)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_017: mol_017 -> mol_018 (Cyclization of GSA to P5C) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_018: mol_018, mol_004 -> mol_012 (Reduction of P5C to proline (speculative)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_019: mol_019 -> mol_012 (Hydrothermal cyclization/pyrolysis: ornithine to proline) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_020: mol_020 -> mol_019 (Hydrothermal deamination: arginine to ornithine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_021: mol_016 -> mol_019 (Hydrothermal rearrangement: glutamate to ornithine) [Hydrothermal]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Cyanosulfidic photoredox route to proline (Patel et al.) (8 steps)\n  - P2: Cyanosulfidic\u2013\u03b2-alanine side branch (4 steps)\n  - P3: Competing arginine branch (guanidinylation) (4 steps)\n  - P4: Meteorite/ice delivery and post-hydrolysis release of proline (2 steps)\n  - P5: Spark discharge Strecker chemistry route (inferred) (2 steps)\n  - P6: Parent-body aqueous alteration (meteorite) (2 steps)\n  - P7: Metabolism-first: glutamate pathway (speculative beyond Glu) (4 steps)\n  - P8: Hydrothermal ornithine/arginine \u2192 proline cyclization (pyrolysis) (2 steps)\n  - P9: Hydrothermal rearrangement: glutamate to ornithine to proline (3 steps)\n  - P10: Chiral phase-behavior amplification to L-proline (1 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, 