8,\n      \"feedback\": \"This 'arginine branch' is chemically plausible up to the arginine aminonitrile, with guanidinylation supported by the literature. However, hydrolysis steps (rxn_014, 020 and 019) are unbalanced and lack experimental evidence for hydrothermal, nonenzymatic Arg/Orn\u2192Pro conversion. The pathway correctly reflects cyanamide as a competing branch; however, steps after arginine lack validation and violate mass/charge balance.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_013\", \"rxn_014\", \"rxn_020\", \"rxn_019\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Clarify all byproducts and attempt to balance hydrolysis/cyclization reactions.\",\n        \"Explicitly label steps beyond arginine as speculative in a nonenzymatic context.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_021\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.5,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.6,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.62,\n      \"feedback\": \"This pathway reflects the detected presence of proline in extraterrestrial residue after hydrolysis, not a demonstrated abiotic route. Both steps are atom/charge unbalanced and mechanistically ill-defined: rxn_010 in particular does not conserve C/H/N, and proline must be released from unknown precursors rather than formed directly. This is a valid 'detection route,' but not a mechanistic synthesis.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_010\", \"rxn_021\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Express these as detection events, not as synthetic steps.\",\n        \"Clarify the unknown nature of the precursor(s) and avoid implying mechanistic detail where none exists.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.7\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.65,\n      \"feedback\": \"This spark discharge Strecker pathway reflects the literature detection of proline in Miller-type experiments. However, the steps are grossly unbalanced as written (rxn_011: not all C/H/N accounted for) and lack characterized intermediates specific to proline (e.g., pyrroline intermediates are only inferred). This aligns with literature as a detection route but does not constitute a valid stepwise synthesis.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_011\", \"rxn_008\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Clearly designate these as detection-only where intermediate mechanisms are undemonstrated.\",\n        \"Supply speculative, balanced intermediates if possible or refrain from mechanistic detail.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_012\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.7\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.65,\n      \"feedback\": \"This parent-body aqueous alteration route is literature accurate as a detection pathway, but the actual steps (rxn_012, rxn_008) are highly unbalanced and not mechanistically justified for proline. The route is included correctly as a detection outcome, but should not imply stepwise synthesis where none exists.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_012\", \"rxn_008\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Present this as a detection outcome, not a resolved pathway.\",\n        \"Clarify that the chemistries operating on parent bodies lack proline-specific mechanistic data.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_015\": 0.7,\n        \"rxn_016\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_017\": 0.6,\n        \"rxn_018\": 0.5\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.55,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.6,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.85,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.62,\n      \"feedback\": \"This speculative 'metabolism-first' pathway is correctly marked as hypothetical in the literature. Reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoglutarate to glutamate is shown experimentally under hydrothermal/mild aqueous conditions; however, all subsequent steps to proline (reduction and cyclization of GSA/P5C, reduction to proline) have not been demonstrated abiotically. Atom-balance is poor in all but the first step. The pathway's inclusion is valid for completeness but does not represent a feasible synthetic route at present.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_016\", \"rxn_017\", \"rxn_018\"],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Explicitly label the Glu\u2192Pro portion as speculative and undemonstrated.\",\n        \"Attempt to achieve atom balance if further mechanistic proposals are made.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_020\": 0.5,\n        \"rxn_019\": 0.6\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.55,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.6,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.85,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.62,\n      \"feedback\": \"The hydrothermal ornithine/arginine \u2192 proline branch correctly models literature indications of Arg/Orn conversion to proline under pyrolytic/hydrothermal conditions, but as per K\u00f6rner et al. 2021 and Vallentyne 1968, the product identity is not secure and experimental demonstration is lacking. Both steps are unbalanced. This is a speculative/degradation pathway, valid for inclusion but not viable as a robust synthetic path.\",\n      