c demonstration; step is thermodynamically uphill and unproven\u2014annotated as speculative (see literature review, Section 5, and Fichman et al. 2015)."}, {"id": "rxn_013", "name": "Spontaneous cyclization of GSA to P5C", "inputs": ["C5H9NO3"], "outputs": ["mol_017", "H2O"], "environment": "Hydrothermal", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "RT\u2013370K", "pressure": "high or moderate", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": null}, "mechanism": "GSA spontaneously cyclizes nonenzymatically to the cyclic imine P5C.", "reasoning": "Supported by reports from Smith & Greenberg (1956). No prebiotic reduction for next step is known."}, {"id": "rxn_014", "name": "Speculative reduction of P5C to proline (not experimentally demonstrated)", "inputs": ["mol_017", "H2"], "outputs": ["mol_011"], "environment": "Hydrothermal", "agents": ["Fe0/Ni0/FeS meteorite minerals"], "conditions": {"temperature": "RT\u2013370K", "pressure": "high/ambient", "catalyst": "nonenzymatic metal", "aqueous": true, "other": null}, "mechanism": "Reduction of the cyclic imine to secondary amine (proline).", "reasoning": "No prebiotic reduction for P5C to proline is published; this is labeled speculative (see literature and Fichman et al. 2015)."}, {"id": "rxn_015", "name": "Strecker synthesis via 4-aminobutanal (spark discharge scenario, detection route)", "inputs": ["mol_006", "mol_001", "mol_003"], "outputs": ["mol_009", "mol_020"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": ["spark discharge, silicate minerals"], "conditions": {"temperature": "300-370K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": "high-voltage discharge", "aqueous": true, "other": "strongly reducing atmosphere"}, "mechanism": "Assembly and Strecker cyanation of 4-aminobutanal yields cyclic \u03b1-aminonitrile.", "reasoning": "No intermediates isolated, detection of proline after hydrolysis is established (Ring et al. 1972; Miller & Urey lineage; Johnson et al. 2008; detection, not stepwise confirmation)."}, {"id": "rxn_016", "name