m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: L-Proline\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The network includes both mechanistically-resolved and detection-based prebiotic routes to proline, using the only demonstrated stepwise route (Patel et al., 2015, Nature Chem.) as the backbone. Ten distinct pathways cover: (1) cyanosulfidic surface photoredox, (2) arginine/ornithine branch cyclization, (3) spark discharge Strecker, (4) interstellar ice photolysis, (5) parent-body alteration in meteorites/asteroids, (6) nebular FTT catalysis, (7) surface Strecker via 4-aminobutanal, (8) hypothetical protometabolic glutamate/P5C reduction, (9) phase-behavior chiral amplification, and (10) chirality transfer from sugars or CPL. Atom and charge balance is strictly maintained for all discrete steps; detection-based and hydrolysis routes are explicitly annotated. Each step is justified and citations provided, with all speculative branches declared. Feedstock selection, intermediate assignment, and reaction families are chosen according to experimental evidence and mechanistic constraint.\n\nMOLECULES (20 nodes):\n  - mol_001: HCN (HCN) [starting]\n  - mol_002: C2H2 (acetylene) [starting]\n  - mol_003: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_004: CH2=CHCN (acrylonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: C3H7N (\u03b2-aminoprop